The provided code seems mostly correct. However, the issue might be due to the fact that the OpenAI API has rate limits on the number of requests you can make within a certain time frame. If you're exceeding this limit, you'll get a `RateLimitError`.

To fix the issue, you can try one of the following:

1.  Wait for some time before making the next request to see if the rate limit has expired.
2.  Check your OpenAI plan and billing details to see if you've exceeded your quota.
3.  Consider upgrading your plan to increase your request limit.
4.  You can also try to use the `openai.ApiClient` class to handle the API requests and errors more robustly.

Note: Make sure to replace `<Your_API_Key>` with your actual OpenAI API key.

