Title: Why Enumerator MoveNext() returns 0.
Body: <p>Why next code generates loop hangs?</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var x = new
{
    Items = new List&lt;int&gt; { 1, 2, 3 }.GetEnumerator()
};

while (x.Items.MoveNext())
   Console.WriteLine(x.Items.Current);
</code></pre>
<p>If I get enumerator after x initialization, than everything works fine:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var x = new
{
    Items = new List&lt;int&gt; { 1, 2, 3 }
};

var enumerator = x.Items.GetEnumerator();

while (enumerator.MoveNext())
   Console.WriteLine(enumerator.Current);
</code></pre>
<p>Tried to decompile both code blocks, but don't understand the reason:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>List&lt;int&gt; intList = new List&lt;int&gt;();
intList.Add(1);
intList.Add(2);
intList.Add(3);
var data1 = new \u003C\u003Ef__AnonymousType0&lt;List&lt;int&gt;.Enumerator&gt;(intList.GetEnumerator());
while (true)
{
   List&lt;int&gt;.Enumerator items = data1.Items;
   if (items.MoveNext())
   {
     items = data1.Items;
     Console.WriteLine(items.Current);
   }
   else
     break;
}
List&lt;int&gt; Items = new List&lt;int&gt;();
Items.Add(1);
Items.Add(2);
Items.Add(3);
var data2 = new \u003C\u003Ef__AnonymousType0&lt;List&lt;int&gt;&gt;(Items);
List&lt;int&gt;.Enumerator enumerator = data2.Items.GetEnumerator();
while (enumerator.MoveNext())
   Console.WriteLine(enumerator.Current);
</code></pre>

Answers:
The reason for the loop hang in the first code block is that the enumerator is not moved to the beginning of the collection after the first iteration. When you call `x.Items.MoveNext()`, it only advances the position within the existing enumerator, but it does not reset the position to the beginning of the collection.

Here is the corrected Python code:

```python
x = {
    'Items': list(range(1, 4))
}
for item in x['Items']:
    print(item)
```

In this corrected version, we are using a for loop which automatically advances the position to the beginning of the collection after each iteration.

