Title: Tic-tac-toe: Loading a save from a file.
Body: <p>I have been trying to make a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tic-tac-toe" rel="nofollow noreferrer">tic-tac-toe</a> game, which prints out a board from the users input, and I have managed to save the boards current state, the grid's size, and the round count.
But when I try to load these data, for some reason I can't get the state of the board to be loaded from the .txt file.</p>
<pre><code>void FileLoad(char ***Board, int *x, int *y, int *roundcount, const char *filename) {
    FILE *Load =fopen(filename, &quot;r&quot;);
    if (Load == NULL) {
        printf(&quot;Error&quot;);
        return;
    }

    fscanf(Load, &quot;%d&quot;, *roundcount);
